<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ============================================================
    Pulse — adaptive icon foreground ("P" monogram)

    Design constraints (all driven by Android's adaptive-icon
    rendering model — see mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml):

      1. Viewport is 108dp × 108dp, not 72dp. This is the
         ADAPTIVE ICON canvas size. The visible icon is
         approximately the inner 72dp circle, but the outer
         18dp "bleed" ring on each side is composited for
         launchers that add parallax, shadows, or their own
         decoration.

      2. The mark lives inside the central 66dp circle
         (radius ≈33dp from the icon center at (54,54)).
         This is the "safe zone" guaranteed visible on every
         launcher mask that follows the adaptive icon spec.
         Anything outside radius 33 is cropped by some
         launchers and shown by others — visually
         inconsistent, so we avoid it.

      3. Single white path. The system tints this layer
         however the launcher chooses (white for a default
         icon, wallpaper-palette-tinted when the user enables
         Material You Themed Icons on API 33+). Do not add
         color to the foreground — it is a template, not a
         picture.

      4. Two contours in ONE path, using fillType="evenOdd"
         to cut the bowl's counter (the hole inside the "P")
         out of the filled silhouette. Splitting the counter
         into a separate <path> would require the counter to
         be drawn in the background color, which is not
         portable (the foreground layer has a transparent
         background, not a color).

    Geometry summary (for anyone editing this later — the
    path data is opaque without this reference):

        STEM          x: 38→50  (width 12dp)
        STEM          y: 28→82  (height 54dp)
        BOWL TOP      y: 28
        BOWL BOTTOM   y: 60
        BOWL RIGHT    curve apex ≈ (70, 44)
        COUNTER LEFT  x: 50     (coincides with stem right edge)
        COUNTER TOP   y: 40
        COUNTER BOTTOM y: 52
        COUNTER RIGHT curve apex ≈ (62, 46)

    The counter's left edge sits exactly on the stem's right
    edge (both at x=50) — that adjacency is what makes the
    shape read as a single continuous "P" rather than a stem
    with a detached bowl attached to it.
    ============================================================
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!--
        Outer contour (the "P" silhouette):
            M 38,28         → start top-left of the stem
            L 58,28         → top edge, right to where the
                              bowl begins its curve
            C 74,28 74,60 58,60
                            → outer bowl curve: cubic bezier
                              from (58,28) to (58,60) with
                              control points (74,28) and
                              (74,60). Produces a smooth
                              rightward bulge. Apex is
                              approximately (70, 44).
            L 50,60         → bottom edge of the bowl,
                              returning left to the stem
            L 50,82         → stem continues down to the
                              bottom of the icon canvas
            L 38,82         → bottom of the stem
            Z               → close back to (38,28) —
                              implicit left edge of the stem

        Inner contour (bowl counter / hole):
            M 50,40         → top-left of the counter
            L 56,40         → top of the counter, straight
            C 62,40 62,52 56,52
                            → inner bowl curve, matching the
                              outer curve's shape but scaled
                              down to leave a uniform stroke
                              thickness around the counter
            L 50,52         → bottom of the counter
            Z               → close back to (50,40) —
                              implicit left edge of the
                              counter, coincident with the
                              stem's right edge

        With android:fillType="evenOdd" on this single <path>,
        the two contours produce a solid "P" with a hole in
        the bowl.
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M 38,28 L 58,28 C 74,28 74,60 58,60 L 50,60 L 50,82 L 38,82 Z M 50,40 L 56,40 C 62,40 62,52 56,52 L 50,52 Z" />

</vector>
